[Music]  welcome back to cbs mornings despite  unrelenting defense by ukrainian forces  russia has taken a key city in the  country's south according to a local  official here you can see russian  military trucks and tanks rolling  through the streets of kirsan the city  of nearly 300 000 along the black sea  would be the largest ukrainian city to  fall since the invasion began a week ago  the people of ukraine are not backing  down this video shows hundreds forming a  human wall to stop russian troops from  taking over a nuclear facility  and here unarmed protesters marched with  ukrainian flags even after hearing  russian gunfire think about that for a  second  senator lindsey graham says russian  president vladimir putin should be  investigated for war crimes and he is  urging the senate to pass a resolution  supporting an international criminal  court investigation into putin and his  regime's quote war crimes against  humanity and war crimes against the  people of ukraine and others close quote  and senator graham joins us now senator  graham thank you very much for being  here you've been  one of the most persistent and public  critics of vladimir putin in congress  i'm thinking about you inviting a  dissident not that long ago to actually  testify against him in the united states  congress uh on the war crimes question  what was the breaking point for you  before this extraordinary press  conference yesterday  when they started using uh band  munitions like cluster bombs uh vacuum  bombs everything he's doing is illegal  under the law of war and the  international criminal court during the  balkans conflict really came about  in the 90s and we had 161 people from  privates to prime ministers prosecuted  for war crimes there is no rule of law  in russia to hold putin accountable so  this international tribunal is the right  way to go i talked to the british  yesterday and we're going to come up  with a plan to start  identifying russian units and give the  world the names of the commanders of the  people who are doing this so i want a  multiple front approach when it comes to  putin  and those who are carrying out this war  economic sanctions aid to the ukrainians  so they can fight back but i want every  military commander and every pilot to  know in russia that if you carry out  these atrocities against the ukrainian  people you do so at your own peril  you're going to wind up in the dark  so let's linger on those atrocities for  a second senator because it doesn't take  an expert in military tactics to look at  the putin situation and say he's in  trouble the ukrainian people are putting  up a tremendous fight he's got no way  out it seems except through so this  could get very bad yeah thinking back to  world war ii is there a moment for  americans for the american military  where we say as human beings as people  we can't let this stand anymore we need  to do something in the country  well you know that's a really good  question i'm not supporting ground  american ground forces in ukraine like  everybody else i move to tears by the  ukrainians will to fight the cities will  begin to fall but the insurgency will  linger and this war could go on for a  very long time i'm trying to make it  real to the people carrying out the war  that if you follow putin you could wind  up losing your own freedom so what i  hope will happen here is that the world  not just the american people  will will make a case against putin  that's been unmade for 20 years he has  literally jailed opponents in russia  poisoned people he carpet bombed aleppo  in syria and idlib syria and chechnya  and nothing happened enough is enough  china is watching i want the chinese to  know that if you go down this road with  taiwan you may wind up not only being  sanctioned but going to jail one day  it is shocking senator to watch this in  real time right before our eyes  like you everybody has moved to tears by  what we're seeing in ukraine but you've  said this if putin gets away with this  the u.s will pay a very heavy price so  how far should the us be willing to go  to defend what is happening here yeah i  heard you say no boots on the ground but  how far should we go right  okay the achilles heel of the  putin war machine is oil and gas sector  the byte administration is coming around  to the idea of sanctioning russian oil  and gas it's about 40 of the income of  russia comes from russian oil and gas  four percent of our energy oil comes  from russia we can make that up if we  choose to but every barrel of oil coming  out of russia has blood in it so if you  hit the oil and gas sector that will  further crush the rupal but this front  about legal liability  trust me the people carrying out this  war  need to understand that they're exposed  as individuals so the one thing we could  do that we're not doing is going after  the oil and gas sector and the other  thing is elevate the determination of  the world to hold these people  accountable for committing war crimes  so senator when it comes to the oil and  gas question uh and it's a good one  it presumes that president putin  continues to be a rational actor that he  is not a crazy person that he will back  down if he is threatened financially or  his economy is threatened you've been  watching him for a long time do you  still believe and not everyone does that  he is a rational player in on the world  stage  i think he's got a plan to destroy  ukraine and to bring  certain satellite soviet states back  into his orbit uh in terms of a nuclear  exchange the french had the best answer  we have weapons too and you know nobody  wins a nuclear war so i'm not dr phil i  can't tell you what makes this guy tick  but i can't tell you we can crush the  ruble we can destroy the russian economy  the russian people are not our enemy uh  it is putin we're fighting a man in a in  a small group of people the oligarchs  are beginning to lose their yachts i  want the military commanders to know you  know is this who you want your country  to be are you going to follow this guy  to the gates of hell  there's a chance to break putin from his  people and everything we can do to hurt  the russian economy i hate it for the  russian people makes this more  unsustainable so we got a moment in  history to do something with putin we  haven't done it 20 years put him out of  the game  senator i want to ask you to be dr phil  but i will ask you to predict something  for me you have warned that if ukraine  is successful in standing their ground  that putin will your words go scorched  earth what does that look like do you  believe that he will go beyond ukraine  uh i don't know if you'll go beyond  ukraine but here's what's going to  happen urban warfare is very difficult  we learned that in iraq and afghanistan  so if a sniper shoots a russian soldier  from an apartment building what we would  do is try to isolate the sniper what  they will do is destroy the  apartment building he's going scorched  earth here he's going to start  disassembling all resistance he has no  look at aleppo if you want to know the  playbook for putin checks nia he  leveled the place olympia aleppo  syria barrel bombs coming out of  helicopters that's the russian game plan  and they're all war crimes and the world  complained but we moved on we can't move  on when it comes to ukraine china's  watching iran is watching  yeah senator graham you've had your eyes  focused on putin now for many years we  appreciate you coming on to share your  perspective as this tragedy continues to  unfold please come back to us

